<section id="compare" class="panel active"><div class="section"><div class="ey">CORE RULE</div><h2>Same required body result. Two different routes.</h2><div class="rule">PHARMACY RESULT = ILMB RESULT <small>Equality means the same patient output is measured and matched. A different mechanism is allowed. If equivalent protection has not been demonstrated, the status remains NOT YET ESTABLISHED.</small></div><div class="compare-wrap"><table class="compare"><thead><tr><th>Required body result</th><th>Medicine + dose</th><th>Pharmacy route</th><th>Collateral route</th><th>ILMB route to same result</th><th>Proof / status</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td class="goal">Lower recurrent ischemic / thrombotic risk</td><td><b>Clopidogrel 75 mg</b><br><b>Aspirin 150 mg</b></td><td>P2Y12 inhibition + COX-1/TXA₂ inhibition → platelet activation/aggregation ↓</td><td class="harm">Normal hemostasis is also reduced → bruising/bleeding/GI bleeding burden can increase.</td><td>Reduce measurable non-platelet contributors: BP load, TG-rich particles, atherogenic burden, inactivity, endothelial/metabolic stress; resolve MCA perfusion/collateral state.</td><td><b>NOT YET EQUIVALENT</b><br>Risk contributors can be reduced, but direct antiplatelet recurrence protection is not replaced by assumption.<br><span class="tag">SUPPORTIVE</span></td></tr>
<tr><td class="goal">Lower BP / vascular resistance / workload</td><td><b>Amlodipine 5 mg</b><br><b>Atenolol 50 mg</b></td><td>L-type Ca²⁺ channel blockade → arterial relaxation; β1 blockade → HR/cardiac workload ↓</td><td class="harm">Edema/dizziness/hypotension; bradycardia/fatigue and suppressed exercise-HR response.</td><td>Measure sodium/fluid input, sleep/autonomic state, conditioning, activity and vascular load; change measured contributors one at a time.</td><td>Same 7-day mean SBP/DBP + resting pulse reached reproducibly.<br><span class="tag pink">DIRECTLY TESTABLE</span></td></tr>
<tr><td class="goal">Lower triglyceride-rich particles</td><td><b>Fenofibrate 160 mg</b></td><td>PPARα activation → fatty-acid oxidation/TG clearance pathways ↑</td><td class="harm">Liver/muscle/kidney/gallbladder burden can occur; statin combination increases muscle concern.</td><td>Weighed food chemistry + movement/workload → reduce verified hepatic TG substrate + increase measured utilisation → repeat fasting TG.</td><td>Required fasting TG reduction matched and sustained with acceptable burden.<br><span class="tag pink">DIRECTLY TESTABLE</span></td></tr>
<tr><td class="goal">Lower LDL / non-HDL / apoB burden</td><td><b>Atorvastatin 40 mg</b></td><td>HMG-CoA reductase inhibition in liver → hepatic cholesterol synthesis ↓ → LDL clearance response ↑</td><td class="harm">Muscle and liver adverse-effect pathways are monitored.</td><td>Weighed food chemistry + intestinal/substrate pattern + hepatic substrate supply + activity/body composition → same lipid-output reduction.</td><td>Same LDL-C/non-HDL-C/apoB endpoint matched; molecular route can differ.<br><span class="tag pink">DIRECTLY TESTABLE</span></td></tr>
<tr><td class="goal">Meet nutrient/cofactor requirement without excess</td><td><b>Cod liver oil 300 mg</b><br><b>Neurobion Forte</b></td><td>Fixed nutrient formulation → biochemical exposure</td><td class="harm">Wrong identity, unnecessary dose or interaction can create burden.</td><td>Exact label chemistry + diet chemistry + measured requirement → calculate missing chemical amount only.</td><td>Repeat exact biomarker; no dose equation until formulation identity is verified.<br><span class="tag">BLOCKED UNTIL VERIFIED</span></td></tr>
</tbody></table></div></div></section>
<section id="deep" class="panel"><div class="section"><div class="ey">FULL CAUSAL FLOW</div><h2>Medicine → part affected → normal job → treatment output → collateral branch → ILMB convergence → proof</h2><p class="lead">This is the level the hospital will use for every medicine. ChEBI identifies chemicals, LOINC identifies measurements, therapy modules converge only where they influence the same physiological node, and pH is allowed only when the relevant compartment and mechanism are established.</p><div class="deep">
<details class="drug" open><summary><b>01</b><strong>Clopidogrel 75 mg · Clopilet</strong><span>Primary part: platelet P2Y12 receptor</span><span>Required output: lower pathologic platelet-driven thrombosis risk</span></summary><div class="drug-body"><div class="chain"><div class="node"><b>Medicine + dose</b><p>Clopidogrel 75 mg</p></div><div class="arrow">→</div><div class="node"><b>Part affected</b><p>P2Y12 ADP receptor on platelets</p></div><div class="arrow">→</div><div class="node"><b>Normal job</b><p>Amplifies ADP-driven platelet activation and aggregation during hemostasis.</p></div><div class="arrow">→</div><div class="node black"><b>Drug action</b><p>P2Y12 signalling ↓ → platelet aggregation ↓</p></div><div class="arrow">→</div><div class="node pink"><b>Desired output</b><p>Lower platelet contribution to arterial thrombus formation.</p></div></div><div class="branches"><div class="branch"><h3>WHY THIS HELPS</h3><p>Less platelet aggregation can reduce thrombotic occlusion risk where platelet activation contributes.</p></div><div class="branch"><h3>COLLATERAL BRANCH</h3><p>The same platelets are also needed for normal hemostasis. Suppressing their activation can increase bruising/bleeding burden.</p></div></div><div class="matrix"><div class="cell"><b>ILMB same-output route</b><p>ILMB can reduce other measurable contributors to total vascular risk, but cannot label that as P2Y12-equivalent protection without outcome evidence.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>LOINC / measurements</b><p>CBC/platelets, lipid outputs, BP, recurrent-neurologic events; exact LOINC attached when verified.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>ChEBI / chemistry</b><p>Track chemistry only for verified vascular/metabolic inputs; arachidonic acid ChEBI 15843 is relevant to the neighbouring eicosanoid/TXA₂ branch, not a replacement claim.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Therapy convergence</b><p>Movement, food chemistry, sleep/autonomic work and rehabilitation may reduce non-platelet risk contributors; none is promoted as direct P2Y12 replacement.</p></div></div><div class="call"><b>Equality status:</b> NOT ESTABLISHED for antiplatelet recurrence protection. ILMB is supportive around the same clinical goal until equivalent protection is demonstrated.</div></div></details>
<details class="drug"><summary><b>02</b><strong>Aspirin 150 mg · Ecosprin</strong><span>Primary part: platelet COX-1 → thromboxane pathway</span><span>Required output: lower TXA₂-mediated platelet aggregation</span></summary><div class="drug-body"><div class="chain"><div class="node"><b>Medicine + dose</b><p>Aspirin 150 mg</p></div><div class="arrow">→</div><div class="node"><b>Part affected</b><p>Platelet COX-1 / arachidonic-acid eicosanoid pathway</p></div><div class="arrow">→</div><div class="node"><b>Normal job</b><p>Supports thromboxane generation used for platelet activation and hemostatic clot formation.</p></div><div class="arrow">→</div><div class="node black"><b>Drug action</b><p>COX-1 inhibition → TXA₂ production ↓ → aggregation ↓</p></div><div class="arrow">→</div><div class="node pink"><b>Desired output</b><p>Lower TXA₂-mediated thrombotic platelet activity.</p></div></div><div class="branches"><div class="branch"><h3>WHY THIS HELPS</h3><p>Reduces one platelet route that can participate in arterial thrombosis.</p></div><div class="branch"><h3>COLLATERAL BRANCH</h3><p>Platelet hemostasis falls; gastrointestinal prostaglandin-related protection can also be affected, contributing to irritation/bleeding burden.</p></div></div><div class="matrix"><div class="cell"><b>ILMB same-output route</b><p>Reduce total thrombotic pressure through measurable vascular/metabolic routes. Do not call this COX-1/TXA₂ equivalence.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>LOINC / measurements</b><p>CBC/platelets, bleeding/GI record, BP, lipids and recurrence context.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>ChEBI / chemistry</b><p>Arachidonic acid ChEBI 15843 anchors the eicosanoid chemistry layer; downstream identities require exact governed mapping.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Therapy convergence</b><p>Food chemistry, movement, sleep/autonomic state and vascular rehabilitation can converge on overall risk, not directly on aspirin’s platelet mechanism.</p></div></div><div class="call"><b>Equality status:</b> NOT ESTABLISHED for aspirin-equivalent antiplatelet protection.</div></div></details>
<details class="drug"><summary><b>03</b><strong>Amlodipine 5 mg · Amlodac AT component</strong><span>Primary part: L-type Ca²⁺ channels in vascular smooth muscle</span><span>Required output: lower systemic vascular resistance / BP</span></summary><div class="drug-body"><div class="chain"><div class="node"><b>Medicine + dose</b><p>Amlodipine 5 mg</p></div><div class="arrow">→</div><div class="node"><b>Part affected</b><p>Arterial vascular smooth muscle L-type calcium channels</p></div><div class="arrow">→</div><div class="node"><b>Normal job</b><p>Calcium entry supports smooth-muscle contraction and vascular tone.</p></div><div class="arrow">→</div><div class="node black"><b>Drug action</b><p>Ca²⁺ entry ↓ → arterial contraction ↓ → vasodilation</p></div><div class="arrow">→</div><div class="node pink"><b>Desired output</b><p>Systemic vascular resistance ↓ → BP ↓</p></div></div><div class="branches"><div class="branch"><h3>WHY THIS HELPS</h3><p>Lower pressure reduces vascular load and cardiac afterload.</p></div><div class="branch"><h3>COLLATERAL BRANCH</h3><p>Excess vasodilation can contribute to dizziness/hypotension; arteriolar dilation can contribute to peripheral edema.</p></div></div><div class="matrix"><div class="cell"><b>ILMB same-output route</b><p>Quantify sodium/fluid intake, sleep/autonomic state, conditioning/activity and vascular load. Change one abnormal contributor and repeat the same BP protocol.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>LOINC / measurements</b><p>7-day mean SBP/DBP, pulse, edema/dizziness; laboratory identities attached when relevant.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>ChEBI / chemistry</b><p>Nitric oxide ChEBI 16480 can anchor an endothelial-relaxation chemistry route only where the input→NO→vascular-output chain is verified.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Therapy convergence</b><p>Movement/conditioning, sleep, breathing/yoga or other autonomic approaches can converge on BP only if Nilesh’s measured BP changes under a controlled protocol.</p></div></div><div class="call"><b>Equality test:</b> ILMB succeeds only if the required SBP/DBP output is matched reproducibly, not because a therapy is theoretically “good for BP.”</div></div></details>
<details class="drug"><summary><b>04</b><strong>Atenolol 50 mg · Amlodac AT component</strong><span>Primary part: β1-adrenergic signalling in heart</span><span>Required output: lower resting HR / cardiac workload where required</span></summary><div class="drug-body"><div class="chain"><div class="node"><b>Medicine + dose</b><p>Atenolol 50 mg</p></div><div class="arrow">→</div><div class="node"><b>Part affected</b><p>β1-adrenergic receptors, primarily cardiac signalling</p></div><div class="arrow">→</div><div class="node"><b>Normal job</b><p>Sympathetic β1 signalling increases heart rate and contractile drive during demand.</p></div><div class="arrow">→</div><div class="node black"><b>Drug action</b><p>β1 signalling ↓ → HR/workload ↓</p></div><div class="arrow">→</div><div class="node pink"><b>Desired output</b><p>Lower resting cardiac demand / BP contribution</p></div></div><div class="branches"><div class="branch"><h3>WHY THIS HELPS</h3><p>Reduces sympathetic cardiac drive where lower HR/workload is therapeutically useful.</p></div><div class="branch"><h3>COLLATERAL BRANCH</h3><p>Bradycardia, fatigue, dizziness and blunted exercise-heart-rate response can occur; this matters when exercise dose is interpreted.</p></div></div><div class="matrix"><div class="cell"><b>ILMB same-output route</b><p>Use conditioning/autonomic/sleep routes only after resting HR/BP and functional workload are measured.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>LOINC / measurements</b><p>Resting pulse/BP, fatigue/dizziness, perceived exertion, repeatable workload/function tests.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>ChEBI / chemistry</b><p>No food chemical is treated as a β1 substitute. Chemistry can support upstream autonomic/metabolic state only where mapped.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Therapy convergence</b><p>Conditioning, breathing/yoga, sleep restoration and stress work can converge on autonomic output; EMDR is relevant only if a measured trauma/stress driver exists.</p></div></div><div class="call"><b>Equality test:</b> match the required HR/BP/workload output without assuming β1-receptor equivalence.</div></div></details>
<details class="drug"><summary><b>05</b><strong>Atorvastatin 40 mg · Lipvas</strong><span>Primary part: hepatic HMG-CoA reductase pathway</span><span>Required output: lower LDL / non-HDL / apoB burden</span></summary><div class="drug-body"><div class="chain"><div class="node"><b>Medicine + dose</b><p>Atorvastatin 40 mg</p></div><div class="arrow">→</div><div class="node"><b>Part affected</b><p>Hepatic cholesterol-synthesis pathway</p></div><div class="arrow">→</div><div class="node"><b>Normal job</b><p>Supports endogenous cholesterol synthesis used in membranes and other cholesterol-dependent biology.</p></div><div class="arrow">→</div><div class="node black"><b>Drug action</b><p>HMG-CoA reductase inhibition → hepatic cholesterol synthesis ↓ → LDL-clearance response ↑</p></div><div class="arrow">→</div><div class="node pink"><b>Desired output</b><p>Circulating atherogenic LDL/apoB burden ↓</p></div></div><div class="branches"><div class="branch"><h3>WHY THIS HELPS</h3><p>Lower atherogenic particle burden is the measurable treatment result.</p></div><div class="branch"><h3>COLLATERAL BRANCH</h3><p>Muscle and liver adverse-effect pathways are monitored because the intervention acts on hepatic cholesterol synthesis and systemic exposure.</p></div></div><div class="matrix"><div class="cell"><b>ILMB same-output route</b><p>3 weighed food days → IFCT/USDA → substrate pattern + body composition/activity → controlled input change → repeat LDL/non-HDL/apoB.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>LOINC / measurements</b><p>LDL-C/non-HDL/apoB, TG; ALT LOINC 1742-6; muscle symptoms with CK only when clinically indicated.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>ChEBI / chemistry</b><p>Use exact food chemicals and metabolites from the governed DB; do not infer a chemical effect from a food name alone.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Therapy convergence</b><p>Food chemistry + movement/body composition converge on lipid output. Other modalities are excluded unless they have a measured path to the same endpoint.</p></div></div><div class="call"><b>Equality test:</b> required LDL/non-HDL/apoB reduction must be matched; no HMG-CoA molecular equivalence claim is needed.</div></div></details>
<details class="drug"><summary><b>06</b><strong>Fenofibrate 160 mg</strong><span>Primary part: PPARα-regulated lipid metabolism</span><span>Required output: lower triglyceride-rich particles</span></summary><div class="drug-body"><div class="chain"><div class="node"><b>Medicine + dose</b><p>Fenofibrate 160 mg</p></div><div class="arrow">→</div><div class="node"><b>Part affected</b><p>PPARα-regulated fatty-acid/lipoprotein metabolism</p></div><div class="arrow">→</div><div class="node"><b>Normal job</b><p>Coordinates genes involved in fatty-acid oxidation and triglyceride-rich lipoprotein handling.</p></div><div class="arrow">→</div><div class="node black"><b>Drug action</b><p>PPARα activation → TG handling/clearance pathways ↑</p></div><div class="arrow">→</div><div class="node pink"><b>Desired output</b><p>Fasting triglyceride-rich particle burden ↓</p></div></div><div class="branches"><div class="branch"><h3>WHY THIS HELPS</h3><p>The treatment objective is a lower measured TG-rich lipoprotein burden.</p></div><div class="branch"><h3>COLLATERAL BRANCH</h3><p>Liver enzymes, creatinine/kidney context, muscle symptoms and gallbladder burden are relevant safety branches; statin combination increases muscle concern.</p></div></div><div class="matrix"><div class="cell"><b>ILMB same-output route</b><p>Weighed food chemistry → identify TG-producing substrate load; quantify movement/workload → alter one verified substrate or utilisation input → repeat fasting TG.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>LOINC / measurements</b><p>Triglycerides LOINC 2571-8; ALT 1742-6; creatinine 2160-0; eGFR and movement dose.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>ChEBI / chemistry</b><p>Each dietary substrate/metabolite must map to an exact chemical identity before entering a treatment equation.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Therapy convergence</b><p>Food chemistry and muscle activity are the primary convergence modules. Yoga/other modalities enter only if a quantified pathway reaches TG output.</p></div></div><div class="call"><b>Equality test:</b> same fasting TG output reached and sustained with acceptable safety markers.</div></div></details>
<details class="drug"><summary><b>07</b><strong>Cod liver oil 300 mg + Neurobion Forte</strong><span>Primary part: nutrient/cofactor exposure</span><span>Required output: measured nutrient sufficiency without excess</span></summary><div class="drug-body"><div class="chain"><div class="node"><b>Product + amount</b><p>Cod liver oil 300 mg / Neurobion Forte</p></div><div class="arrow">→</div><div class="node"><b>Part affected</b><p>Nutrient-dependent biochemical pathways</p></div><div class="arrow">→</div><div class="node"><b>Normal job</b><p>Vitamins/fatty acids act as substrates or cofactors in many pathways; exact formulation determines which ones.</p></div><div class="arrow">→</div><div class="node black"><b>Product action</b><p>Fixed chemical exposure</p></div><div class="arrow">→</div><div class="node pink"><b>Desired output</b><p>Correct the specific measured requirement, not “more vitamins.”</p></div></div><div class="branches"><div class="branch"><h3>WHY THIS HELPS</h3><p>Only a demonstrated deficiency/requirement defines the useful output.</p></div><div class="branch"><h3>COLLATERAL BRANCH</h3><p>Unnecessary or excessive intake can create interaction or toxicity burden; exact EPA/DHA/A/D/B-vitamin amounts matter.</p></div></div><div class="matrix"><div class="cell"><b>ILMB same-output route</b><p>Exact label + weighed food chemistry → total chemical intake → measured requirement → fill only the deficit from food and/or supplement.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>LOINC / measurements</b><p>25-OH vitamin D LOINC 62292-8; B12 and other need-specific markers only when relevant.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>ChEBI / chemistry</b><p>Every nutrient must use exact chemical/form identity from the DB before dose arithmetic.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Therapy convergence</b><p>No therapy replaces a missing chemical requirement; therapies may affect symptoms/function but not substitute for an identified biochemical deficit.</p></div></div><div class="call"><b>Equality test:</b> same biomarker/functional requirement reached without excess. Dose remains blocked until exact formulation is verified.</div></div></details>
</div><div class="phgate"><b>pH GATE — NEVER “BODY pH”</b><br>pH enters a treatment flow only as <b>compartment + measured pH + mechanism + output</b>. Blood, urine, gastric lumen and intracellular pH are different systems. For Nilesh’s current BP/lipid/antiplatelet comparison, no pH intervention is promoted unless a compartment-specific abnormality and causal route to the required output are actually measured.</div></div></section>
<section id="path" class="panel"><div class="section"><div class="ey">ACTUAL ILMB PATH</div><h2>Same-output intervention blocks</h2><div class="paths"><details class="path" open><summary><b>01</b><strong>BP / vascular resistance</strong><span>Same output as amlodipine/atenolol goal</span></summary><div class="path-body"><div class="cell"><b>Baseline</b><p>7 days AM+PM BP/pulse; 2 readings after 5 min seated.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Input map</b><p>Weighed sodium/fluid, sleep, movement, autonomic symptoms.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Intervention</b><p>Change one measured abnormal contributor only.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Re-measure</b><p>Repeat same 7-day protocol.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Decision</b><p>KEEP / MODIFY / INVESTIGATE based on same endpoint.</p></div></div></details><details class="path"><summary><b>02</b><strong>Triglycerides</strong><span>Same output as fenofibrate goal</span></summary><div class="path-body"><div class="cell"><b>Baseline</b><p>Repeat fasting TG + safety labs.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Input map</b><p>3 weighed food days + movement workload.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Intervention</b><p>Change one verified substrate/activity input.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Re-measure</b><p>Repeat fasting TG under same conditions.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Decision</b><p>Compute Nilesh’s ΔTG / verified Δinput.</p></div></div></details><details class="path"><summary><b>03</b><strong>LDL / apoB burden</strong><span>Same output as atorvastatin goal</span></summary><div class="path-body"><div class="cell"><b>Baseline</b><p>LDL-C, non-HDL-C, apoB where available.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Input map</b><p>Food chemistry + body composition/activity.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Intervention</b><p>Alter one verified substrate/metabolic route.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Re-measure</b><p>Repeat same lipid outputs.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Decision</b><p>Judge endpoint equality, not molecular equivalence.</p></div></div></details><details class="path"><summary><b>04</b><strong>Brain perfusion / function</strong><span>Protect tissue and function</span></summary><div class="path-body"><div class="cell"><b>Baseline</b><p>Resolve MCA flow/collaterals/perfusion + grip/gait/strength/dexterity/balance.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Input map</b><p>Perfusion, BP, fatigue, workload.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Intervention</b><p>Task-specific rehab where reserve/deficit exists.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Re-measure</b><p>Repeat identical functional tests.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Decision</b><p>Improve/maintain function; antiplatelet equivalence remains separate.</p></div></div></details></div></div></section>
<section id="reports" class="panel"><div class="section"><div class="ey">REPORTS</div><h2>What happened and what remains unresolved</h2><div class="timeline"><div class="event"><div><b>23 Aug 2024</b><p>MRI</p></div><div><strong>Finding</strong><p>Multiple fresh non-haemorrhagic right fronto-parieto-temporal infarcts.</p></div><div><strong>Meaning</strong><p>Several right-brain regions were injured because blood supply failed.</p></div></div><div class="event"><div><b>23 Aug 2024</b><p>MRA</p></div><div><strong>Finding</strong><p>High-grade right MCA occlusion from origin; severe distal paucity.</p></div><div><strong>Meaning</strong><p>Main arterial route to a large right-brain territory was severely compromised.</p></div></div><div class="event"><div><b>21 Jul 2025</b><p>MRI/MRA</p></div><div><strong>Finding</strong><p>Right MCA M1 no flow; faint M2 enhancement possibly collateral.</p></div><div><strong>Meaning</strong><p>Vessel abnormality persisted; collateral supply may exist but was not quantified.</p></div></div><div class="event"><div><b>26 Jul 2025</b><p>Clinical</p></div><div><strong>Finding</strong><p>Normal speech; no recorded deficit.</p></div><div><strong>Meaning</strong><p>Function recovered more than vessel imaging alone suggests.</p></div></div><div class="event"><div><b>31 Jul 2026</b><p>CT</p></div><div><strong>Finding</strong><p>Old right-sided infarcts; no acute infarct, haemorrhage or mass.</p></div><div><strong>Meaning</strong><p>No new acute lesion; current MCA lumen/collateral reserve/perfusion remains unresolved.</p></div></div></div></div></section>
<section id="numbers" class="panel"><div class="section"><div class="ey">MEASUREMENTS</div><h2>Numbers that drive the comparison</h2><div class="metrics"><div class="metric"><small>Triglycerides</small><strong>301 mg/dL</strong><small>LOINC 2571-8</small></div><div class="metric"><small>ALT</small><strong>81 U/L</strong><small>LOINC 1742-6</small></div><div class="metric"><small>Creatinine</small><strong>1.27 mg/dL</strong><small>LOINC 2160-0</small></div><div class="metric"><small>eGFR</small><strong>72</strong><small>Kidney context</small></div><div class="metric"><small>Potassium</small><strong>5.3 mmol/L</strong><small>LOINC 2823-3</small></div><div class="metric"><small>Platelets</small><strong>133 ×10³/µL</strong><small>LOINC 777-3</small></div><div class="metric"><small>25-OH Vitamin D</small><strong>13.9 ng/mL</strong><small>LOINC 62292-8</small></div><div class="metric"><small>TSH</small><strong>5.386</strong><small>LOINC 3016-3</small></div><div class="metric"><small>HbA1c</small><strong>5.8%</strong><small>LOINC 4548-4</small></div></div><div class="call"><b>Still unresolved:</b> current right-MCA flow/perfusion/collaterals, repeat fasting labs, quantitative motor baseline, exact cod-liver-oil/Neurobion chemistry, and any compartment-specific pH abnormality relevant enough to enter a treatment equation.</div></div></section>
<section id="science" class="panel"><div class="section"><div class="ey">EVIDENCE LAYER</div><h2>How ChEBI, LOINC, Reactome, therapies and pH converge</h2><div class="flow"><span class="node">Medicine</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="node">Target</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="node">Target job</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="node">Required output</span><span class="arr">=</span><span class="node pink">ILMB output</span></div><div class="flow" style="margin-top:8px"><span class="node">Patient input</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="node">ChEBI chemical identity</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="node">Reactome/pathway node</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="node">Body output</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="node">LOINC / functional measurement</span></div><div class="chem" style="margin-top:9px"><span class="chip pink">ChEBI 16480 · nitric oxide</span><span class="chip pink">ChEBI 15843 · arachidonic acid</span><span class="chip">ChEBI 17968 · butyrate</span><span class="chip">ChEBI 16828 · L-tryptophan</span><span class="chip">LOINC 2571-8 · triglycerides</span><span class="chip">LOINC 1742-6 · ALT</span><span class="chip">LOINC 2160-0 · creatinine</span><span class="chip">LOINC 777-3 · platelets</span></div><div class="matrix"><div class="cell"><b>Food chemistry</b><p>grams × composition → exact chemical input → pathway → output</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Physiotherapy / rehab</b><p>task-specific dose → function/network adaptation → repeat same functional output</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Yoga / breathing / sleep</b><p>only enter where autonomic/BP/sleep output is measured</p></div><div class="cell"><b>EMDR / stress modalities</b><p>only enter where a measured stress/trauma driver connects to autonomic or behavioural output</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Acupuncture / other modalities</b><p>only converge on a physiological node where evidence and patient measurement support the link</p></div><div class="cell"><b>pH</b><p>compartment-specific only: blood ≠ urine ≠ gastric ≠ intracellular; no generic alkalising claim</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Equality gate</b><p>same endpoint + same measurement method + controlled input + repeat response</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Safety gate</b><p>benefit is never accepted while collateral markers worsen without review</p></div></div><div class="call"><b>Governance:</b> no same-endpoint measurement = no Pharmacy=ILMB equality claim. Unknown is never converted to zero. ChEBI/LOINC identities must be verified before arithmetic. pH must specify compartment. Therapy convergence must terminate at a measured body output.</div></div></section>
</div></main><script>const bs=[...document.querySelectorAll('[data-panel]')],ps=[...document.querySelectorAll('.panel')];function show(id){bs.forEach(b=>b.classList.toggle('active',b.dataset.panel===id));ps.forEach(p=>p.classList.toggle('active',p.id===id));history.replaceState(null,'','#'+id)}bs.forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>show(b.dataset.panel));const h=location.hash.slice(1);if(document.getElementById(h))show(h);</script></body></html>